<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milo Đukanović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Milo Đukanović is a Montenegrin politician who dominated the country for three decades, serving several times as prime minister from 1991 and as president in 1998–2002 and 2018–2023. In the late 1990s he broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slobodan-milosevic">Slobodan Milošević</a> and adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deutsche-mark">Deutsche Mark</a> and later the euro, and he led Montenegro to independence after the 2006 referendum and into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 2017.</p></div>
